# Shell scripts must keep LF endings.
#
# core.autocrlf=true is set on the machine these were written on, so a fresh
# Windows clone would otherwise check tool/*.sh out with CRLF -- and bash
# fails on the carriage returns with errors like `$'\r': command not found`,
# which is a confusing way to discover that a release build script is broken.
*.sh text eol=lf
